examples.question_text:
Calculate the area of each shape.
(a) The rectangle
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.38]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (13,6);
\draw (0.45,0)--(0.45,0.45)--(0,0.45);
\node[below] at (6.5,0) {$13\text{ mm}$};
\node[right] at (13,3) {$6\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) The square
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,8);
\draw (0.45,0)--(0.45,0.45)--(0,0.45);
\draw (3.8,-0.14)--(4.2,0.14);
\draw (3.8,7.86)--(4.2,8.14);
\draw (-0.14,3.8)--(0.14,4.2);
\draw (7.86,3.8)--(8.14,4.2);
\node[right] at (8,4) {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Rectangle A measures $8\text{ cm}$ by $3\text{ cm}$. Square B has side length $5\text{ cm}$. Which has the larger area, and by how many square centimetres?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.5cm]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (8,3);
\path (4,0) node[below] {$8\text{ cm}$} (8,1.5) node[right] {$3\text{ cm}$} (4,3) node[above] {A};
\draw[black] (12,0) rectangle (17,5);
\draw[black] (14.5,-0.15)--(14.5,0.15) (14.5,4.85)--(14.5,5.15) (11.85,2.5)--(12.15,2.5) (16.85,2.5)--(17.15,2.5);
\path (14.5,-0.15) node[below] {$5\text{ cm}$} (14.5,5.15) node[above] {B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
